debugfs: report the raw DVFS signal

Measurement support. The load counters are only read by devfreq, and devfreq
only reads them under a polling governor, so with the userspace governor
selected there is no way to see what the driver considers busy - which is the
one thing worth knowing before choosing a governor policy.

Add a "dvfs" node reporting, per core, the cumulative busy count, the pending
task count and whether a job is on the hardware, plus the current rate and
voltage and the last sample devfreq was handed. The busy counts are monotonic,
so a reader takes two samples and divides by the elapsed timestamp; that works
at any interval and does not require a governor to be polling.

npu_core_busy_cum() stops being static so the node computes busy time exactly
the way the governor does, rather than a second implementation that can drift.

Signed-off-by: Isaiah DeRose-Wilson <isaiahdw@gmail.com>

